<%- /*
Scaffolded as rustfmt.toml by rust-systems (internal/flavor/definitions.go). cargo fmt passes each
crate's edition to rustfmt, but rustfmt run directly reads the edition from this file, so the two
disagree on every crate whose edition this file does not name. The edition is therefore the one
every crate of the root Cargo.toml's workspace is on, the root package and each member
(.RustEdition, internal/flavor/rustfmt.go), and the key is left out when none declares one, since
Cargo and rustfmt then both use 2015. Where the crates share no edition, or their editions cannot
be read (no root Cargo.toml among them), the file is not scaffolded. The 2021 and 2024 renderings are byte for byte the texts earlier releases wrote
unconditionally, recorded in priorRustfmtDigests so adoption refreshes an unedited copy
(TestRustfmtPriorTextsAreEarlierRenderings, internal/flavor/rustfmt_test.go).
*/ -%>
<% if .RustEdition -%>
edition = "<% .RustEdition %>"
<% end -%>
max_width = 100
newline_style = "Unix"
use_small_heuristics = "Default"
